1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,600
China paved a road across shifting sand.
I'm your China Travel Expert.

2
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:05,000
The Tarim Desert Highway: 446 km of dunes.

3
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:07,400
The world's longest road across moving sand.

4
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:09,800
Sand buries roads. So they grew a forest.

5
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:12,200
A green belt runs 436 km beside it.

6
00:00:12,200 --> 00:00:14,600
Fed by wells pumped from under the desert.

7
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:16,800
Double-tap if you'd drive this.

8
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:19,200
Workers live out here to keep the sand off.

9
00:00:19,200 --> 00:00:22,000
★ Expert Tip: cross with a local driver — no fuel or water for hours.

10
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:24,600
So: would you drive 446 km of sand? Tell me.
